# The table of built-ins says of the object behind `process.env` that its names hold texts alone. Anybody may put another object in its place or lay something else on it by a descriptor, so nothing is proven of a
# read off it. What was seen is a text or nothing; all the rest is unknown by escape alone. So the reading that says what is expected gives the two functions a result, and their callers test for it.
# RUN: link functions held mechanisms=all
# REQUIRES: entries-of-bun
# CHECK: function f1 {{*}} result=undefined|string
# CHECK: function f2 {{*}} result=undefined|string
# The proving reading says what it said: nothing.
# RUN(PROVEN): link functions mechanisms=all
# REQUIRES(PROVEN): entries-of-bun
# PROVEN-NOT: function f1 {{*}} result=
# PROVEN-NOT: function f2 {{*}} result=
# RUN(WALK): walk f3 mechanisms=all
# REQUIRES(WALK): entries-of-bun
# WALK: TypeTest {{*}} testedType=string
# WALK: GetStringLength
